      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The NMDA receptor has been reported to be involved in opioid tolerance. Adjuvant subcutaneous infusion treatment with (very) low-dose ketamine, a NMDA receptor antagonist, improves analgesia and at the same time appears to reduce morphine tolerance. Three cases are presented."},
